3.2,Video Polls,2018-10-23,,,"
_These changes apply to v3.2+_

You can now create and manage Video Polls on Live Videos and VODs. The following endpoints have been added:

- [`/{video-id}/polls`](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video/polls)
- [`/{live-video-id}/polls`](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/live-video/polls)
- [`/{video-poll-id}`](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video-poll)
- [`/{video-poll-id}/options`](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video-poll/poll_options)
- [`/{video-poll-option-id}`](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/video-poll-option)

Refer to the [Live Polls API documentation](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/videos/live-video/live-polls-api) for usage instructions.

",addition
2.10,Graph API,2017-07-18,New Features,Webhooks,"
- **Webhooks for Page Events** - The following actions will now trigger an update for Page `feed` field subscriptions:

- Auto-publishing a scheduled event
- Commenting on the event story  
- Creating and publishing an event
- Publishing a draft event


",addition
9.0,Marketing API,2020-11-10,Bidding,Deprecated Billing and Optimization Option,"
_Applies to v9.0+_

Starting with v9.0, CPA billing for app ads is deprecated, you cannot set both billing event and optimization goal to `APP_INSTALLS`. Instead, we recommend using the `impression` billing events.

You can still specify `APP_INSTALLS` under `billing_event` or `optimization_goal`, but not both at the same time.


",removal
5.0,Messenger,2019-10-29,New Features,,"
_These changes apply to all versions._

- [Click to Messenger Ads support for Handover protocol](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/ads-commerce/marketing-api/ad-creative/messaging-ads/click-to-messenger). Ads can now indicate the app id that will have control over the thread once a user clicks on the ad.
- [Replies and Reactions Webhooks](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/messenger-platform/webhooks). It is now possible to receive webhook events when users react or reply to  messages from businesses.
- [`POST / GET / DELETE /{page-id}/messenger_profile` — Ice Breakers](https://developers.facebook.com/documentation/business-messaging/messenger-platform/reference/messenger-profile-api/ice-breakers). Apps can now set icebreakers on the Messenger profile via the API to provide a set of common questions that users can use to start a conversation.
- [`GET /{thread-id}` — Admin Messages Filter](https://developers.facebook.com/docs/graph-api/reference/v4.0/thread#filters). Apps can now filter out admin messages to just get messages between the Page and the user.

",addition
